    "body": "# Bug report\n\n### Bug description:\n\nI'm trying to enable TSAN on a local build on Ubuntu 22.04 using the system clang, and I get this weird error:\n```console\n$ CC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --with-thread-sanitizer --with-pydebug --disable-ipv6\n[...]\nchecking for acosh... no\nconfigure: error: Python requires C99 compatible libm\n```\n\nStrangely, this is the same configuration (Ubuntu 22.04, system clang) that works on the Github Actions CI.\n\n\n### CPython versions tested on:\n\nCPython main branch\n\n### Operating systems tested on:\n\nLinux",
